WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.640
Frank Herbert's "Dune" series deals with&nbsp;
the plight of the Fremen people and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.360
struggle to stop intergalactic overlords&nbsp;
from mining their planet to death. The Fremen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.320
serve as "Dune's" emotional center and provide&nbsp;
its narrative backbone. This is their story.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.480
Frank Herbert didn't create this&nbsp;
desert culture out of whole cloth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.720
He drew inspiration from a healthy mix&nbsp;
of world religions and several actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.360
indigenous cultures on Earth. In particular,&nbsp;
he looked at the way that these peoples managed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.680
to make a life for themselves in places&nbsp;
that might be considered inhospitable.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.840
Herbert was compelled to write Dune after&nbsp;
hearing of a project by the United States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.560
Department of Agriculture that would stop&nbsp;
Oregon's marching sand dunes from moving.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.120
The USDA planted different kinds of grass&nbsp;
along the dunes to calm their movements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.040
as the blowing sand could wreak&nbsp;
havoc on nearby roadways and towns.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.400
Herbert decided to contrast the&nbsp;
government's response of changing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.160
the landscape with the way that native&nbsp;
people across Earth have historically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.360
learned to live in harmony with&nbsp;
the planet's natural processes.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.920
The Empire of Dune came to represent these&nbsp;
outsiders reshaping worlds in ways that make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:09.200
them more profitable, while the Fremen stood in&nbsp;
for the ideas of harmonious living. Herbert based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:14.560
the Fremen in large part on the San people who&nbsp;
live in the Kalahari desert. Like the Fremen, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.520
San learned to conserve water in order to survive&nbsp;
in some of the most unforgiving terrain on Earth.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.120
The Fremen are descendants of a persecuted&nbsp;
religious group called the Zensunni Wanderers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.480
This nomadic group fled across the void of space&nbsp;
to evade imperial violence. Herbert created their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.360
religion from the combined tenets of Sunni&nbsp;
Islam and his own belief in Zen Buddhism.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.280
Their final stop was Arrakis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.640
a barren desert planet believed to be worthless&nbsp;
before the discovery of a spice called melange.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.320
"He who controls the spice controls the universe!"

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.800
This spice gave all who consumed it a minor&nbsp;
amount of prescience. It quickly became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.440
crucial for navigating ships in a galaxy&nbsp;
that had created faster-than-light travel.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.160
So, the Fremen found themselves in a familiar&nbsp;
situation to anyone who knows about the Amazon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.480
rainforest or the so-called American&nbsp;
frontier. They were the people living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:09.120
on top of a coveted natural resource, and they&nbsp;
suffered in similar ways to those indigenous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.880
peoples on Earth.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.920
The Fremen were viewed as backward and savage&nbsp;
by Dune-colonizing outsiders. Their culture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.720
was an example of the ways in which humanity&nbsp;
can survive in the least probable situations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:25.120
Because of the extreme scarcity of water on&nbsp;
the surface of their planet, a huge chunk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:30.480
of Fremen culture and ritual is based around the&nbsp;
collection and conservation of this vital mineral.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.120
They travel the surface of Dune dressed in&nbsp;
stillsuits, full-body coverings that collect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.080
and filter sweat, respiratory droplets,&nbsp;
and waste, and store it in catch-pockets.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.720
This water is then recycled via tubes that are&nbsp;
pumped through levers in the stillsuit's heels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.240
In this perfectly closed system,&nbsp;
not a drop of water is wasted.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.720
The Fremen conception of wealth also revolves&nbsp;
around the collection of water. They live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:57.600
in small bands that move between underground&nbsp;
sietches, where they store their water communally.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:02.400
Individuals wear jewelry that symbolize their&nbsp;
share of the water. When Fremen die, their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.440
bodies are rendered in a holy ceremony, and their&nbsp;
water is added back to the wealth of the tribe.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.160
The Fremen have also managed a cautious&nbsp;
coexistence with the desert's greatest threat:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.280
sandworms. Called "makers" by the Fremen, the&nbsp;
massive creatures tunnel through the desert sand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.200
and appear at the slightest noise. Fremen&nbsp;
learn at a young age how to walk through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.840
the desert in a sliding, arrhythmic gait&nbsp;
that mimics the natural settling of sand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.320
They do this to avoid drawing sandworm attention&nbsp;
— unless they're looking to hitch a ride.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:34.560
That's right: The Fremen also have a&nbsp;
strategy for riding the sandworms of Dune.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.720
It's a dangerous maneuver that allows them&nbsp;
to cover massive stretches of the desert at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.560
a clip. This technique is a closely&nbsp;
guarded secret of their community.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.600
Though the Empire believes&nbsp;
that they are few in number,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.040
the truth is that a massive society&nbsp;
has blended into the desert.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.160
"My Lord, I suspect an incredible&nbsp;
secret has been kept on this planet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.400
that the Fremen exist in vast numbers."

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.480
From the safety of their underground sietches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.560
the collected Fremen have been working&nbsp;
on a generational terraforming project.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.120
Their goal is to eventually transform&nbsp;
Dune into a verdant and hospitable planet.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:14.320
This secret society of desert nomads provides&nbsp;
an army lying in wait for Paul Atreides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:19.120
who assumes the Fremen name Muad'dib, to&nbsp;
invade the polar port city of Arrakeen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.680
In the real world, mu'addib is Arabic for teacher.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.920
During the epic Dune saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:28.400
an imperial governor on Dune is overthrown&nbsp;
by a scheming family looking to settle a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.120
blood feud. The son of that governor escapes to&nbsp;
the desert with his mother, the Lady Jessica.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.040
Jessica takes advantage of prophecies&nbsp;
that had been seeded among the Fremen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.040
by a holy order known as the Bene&nbsp;
Gesserit to which she belongs.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.160
Using this Missionaria Protectiva, she coerces&nbsp;
the Fremen into accepting her son as their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:52.000
messiah. His name is Paul Atreides, but he quickly&nbsp;
assumes a Fremen name meaning "kangaroo mouse."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:56.160
The Fremen admire this creature for its&nbsp;
ability to live on the surface of Dune.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:00.400
It's Paul's reciprocal embrace of Fremen&nbsp;
traditions that leads him to the spice and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.320
the awakening of his dormant powers&nbsp;
of prescience. Without the Fremen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.680
Paul and Jessica might never have&nbsp;
survived their exile to the desert.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.280
They certainly wouldn't have been able to&nbsp;
mount an assault on Harkonnen Arrakeen.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.160
Paul became a true messianic figure&nbsp;
during his time among the Fremen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.680
The boy had been trained by his mother&nbsp;
in the weird arts of observation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:24.400
perception, and control practiced by the&nbsp;
Bene Gesserit witches for generations.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:30.000
This all-woman mystical order exerts influence&nbsp;
by subtly molding the genealogy of Great Houses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.440
They then insert their converts into&nbsp;
bloodlines in the hopes of creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:37.520
their own messiah known as the Kwisatz&nbsp;
Haderach. This figure would be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.840
to access areas of prescience that the&nbsp;
Bene Gesserit witches could not reach.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.000
"This is the place they cannot look."

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:49.200
In short, generations of witches had worked to&nbsp;
eventually create a son who would be trained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.360
in their ways. Though Paul's mother had&nbsp;
not been given the go-ahead to train Paul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:58.000
she trained him anyway knowing that he would be&nbsp;
killed by the forces allied against their family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.160
if he was not prescient. When these powers&nbsp;
combined with Paul's training as a Fremen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.960
he became a mystic desert dweller who could&nbsp;
see the future and use it to reshape Dune.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.480
Paul then uses an army of Fremen,&nbsp;
who heard his revolutionary message,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:14.080
to destroy the precious spice&nbsp;
that facilitates all space travel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:19.520
He simultaneously attacks the Empire's outposts,&nbsp;
while holding the galaxy's spice supply hostage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.640
The Emperor is forced to cave to Paul Muad'Dib,&nbsp;
who becomes the undisputed ruler of Dune.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:28.800
Even though Paul is revered as a&nbsp;
god in the flesh by the Fremen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:33.440
history quickly slips out of his control. The&nbsp;
reverence and religious fervor surrounding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:39.440
Muad'Dib transforms into a cosmic jihad waged in&nbsp;
Paul's name. It's fought and led almost entirely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:44.880
by his army of Fremen fedaykin warriors with the&nbsp;
backing of his religious order, the Qizarate.&nbsp;

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.800
Hundreds of worlds and billions of people&nbsp;
come under the sway of Paul's empire in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.280
early days of his reign. A religion grows&nbsp;
around him and the Fremen homeworld of Dune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:57.360
becomes a kind of space-age Jerusalem.&nbsp;
Paul's prescience shows him where this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:03.040
path is headed. But he becomes hemmed in by his&nbsp;
future visions and his status as the godhead. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.000
Paul is essentially paralyzed to act in any way&nbsp;
that might assure his people's enduring salvation.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:13.360
Among the Fremen, there is an undercurrent&nbsp;
of dissent from older veterans of Paul's war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.480
who don't like the way that&nbsp;
Fremen culture is changing. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.040
Paul makes water more available, older Fremen look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:23.600
on in horror as the strict codes observed&nbsp;
by previous generations begin to disappear.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:26.880
In addition to that, the fedaykin&nbsp;
become disillusioned with the war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.200
effort when they come home to meager pensions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:33.920
and comfortable suburban homes that carry&nbsp;
little trace of the harsh life of the sietch.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:37.760
A plot is hatched among these Fremen&nbsp;
dissenters to assassinate Paul.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.240
These rebels are egged on by the Spacing Guild&nbsp;
who have lost their unfettered access to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.040
spice melange. The Bene Gesserit witches, who&nbsp;
have lost control over their breeding program,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:51.200
also encourage the revolt. Paul sees&nbsp;
these machinations in his visions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:56.320
but has trouble figuring out how to avoid the&nbsp;
plots bearing fruit without causing more misery.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.560
Ultimately, he allows himself to be&nbsp;
grievously wounded by the Fremen dissenters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:05.360
He is blinded by a nuclear blast near the&nbsp;
holy city — an attack that he foresaw. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:08.880
strict Fremen way of life holds&nbsp;
that anyone who loses their sight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:14.000
must wander out into the desert and allow himself&nbsp;
to die, rather than slowing down the tribe.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.120
Though Paul is an emperor and could&nbsp;
have carried on without his sight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.920
he sees in this path a way off the treadmill&nbsp;
carrying him toward the Fremen's ultimate demise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.880
In sacrificing himself pursuant to traditional&nbsp;
Fremen law, he silences the doubts of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:30.560
traditionalist hardliners who worried that&nbsp;
he had forgotten the ways of the Fremen.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:37.360
Under the 3,500-year reign of Paul's son&nbsp;
Leto II, the Fremen culture grows faint.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:41.360
By merging with sand trout, a kind of&nbsp;
larval stage of the great sandworms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:47.120
Leto II becomes a nearly immortal human-sandworm&nbsp;
hybrid. He rules long enough to realize the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.840
great dream of Liet-Kynes to terraform&nbsp;
Dune into a moist, temperate planet.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.800
Leto is ultimately killed&nbsp;
by one of his descendants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.800 --> 00:09:00.320
a Fremen-Atreides named Siona who has evolved&nbsp;
the ability to hide from his power of foresight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:05.520
Siona's assassination of Leto sets off the "Great&nbsp;
Scattering." This is an event that sees the many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.720
peoples of the former empire dispersed in a&nbsp;
galactic diaspora. Without access to the spice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:14.960
they are essentially isolated for thousands&nbsp;
of years on their planetary islands.

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:19.360
When the peoples of the Scattering return,&nbsp;
one particularly violent sect — The Honored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:24.240
Matres — bombards the surface of Dune with&nbsp;
planet-destroying weapons. These weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:29.600
called Obliterators, kill the last remnants of the&nbsp;
Fremen civilization. In Frank Herbert's original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:35.280
series of six novels, only one Fremen escapes the&nbsp;
scouring of Dune. This is a girl named Sheeana,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:40.400
a name derived from the original Fremen "Siona,"&nbsp;
and a mainline descendant of Paul Atreides.

